1
00:00:01,141 --> 00:00:02,151
Just a moment.

2
00:00:04,181 --> 00:00:05,181
Yes, Mother.

3
00:00:06,551 --> 00:00:08,351
What? Seung Ri?

4
00:00:09,091 --> 00:00:10,121
Since when?

5
00:00:10,921 --> 00:00:13,091
What is it? Did something happen to Seung Ri?

6
00:00:14,261 --> 00:00:16,761
Mother, I'm heading over there right now.

7
00:00:16,961 --> 00:00:18,031
Yes.

8
00:00:20,531 --> 00:00:22,931
What's wrong? It seems like something urgent came up.

9
00:00:23,031 --> 00:00:25,471
- Let's go see Chief Seo first. - Okay.

10
00:00:26,801 --> 00:00:28,711
All right. I'm hanging up. I'm on my way.

11
00:00:29,441 --> 00:00:30,641
What's wrong? What is it?

12
00:00:30,771 --> 00:00:33,311
It's our Seung Ri... They said she's disappeared.

13
00:00:34,841 --> 00:00:35,911
What?

14
00:00:39,421 --> 00:00:43,021
(Gangsu Construction)

15
00:00:44,151 --> 00:00:45,151
Hey.

16
00:00:46,191 --> 00:00:48,261
What's wrong? What's going on with him?

17
00:00:49,661 --> 00:00:51,131
They said Manager Seo is missing.

18
00:00:52,731 --> 00:00:54,861
What do you mean, Manager Seo is missing?

19
00:00:55,731 --> 00:00:57,701
Don't tell me it's because of that incident?

20
00:00:59,941 --> 00:01:01,701
Oh, poor Gwon Sik.

21
00:01:01,841 --> 00:01:03,511
Of all people,

22
00:01:03,971 --> 00:01:07,041
to have his own beloved daughter find out his shameful secret.

23
00:01:07,281 --> 00:01:08,281
Oh, dear.

24
00:01:11,851 --> 00:01:13,221
Why are you looking at me like that?

25
00:01:13,621 --> 00:01:17,121
Do you really not feel a shred of guilt?

26
00:01:17,851 --> 00:01:19,661
How can you say something like that?

27
00:01:19,721 --> 00:01:20,721
Lower your voice...

28
00:01:21,991 --> 00:01:23,091
Hold on. Hey.

29
00:01:23,731 --> 00:01:26,061
What do I have to feel guilty about?

30
00:01:27,061 --> 00:01:30,471
Come on. Let's get our facts straight.

31
00:01:31,571 --> 00:01:34,041
I'm not the one who made that decision.

32
00:01:34,041 --> 00:01:35,071
Ko Dae Chi!

33
00:01:36,271 --> 00:01:39,041
This is the office. How dare you call me by my name?

34
00:01:42,181 --> 00:01:46,581
I guess you're starting to have some regrets too?

35
00:01:48,351 --> 00:01:50,151
You said it yourself back then.

36
00:01:50,151 --> 00:01:52,421
That you were the one who brought Gwon Sik to me.

37
00:01:53,121 --> 00:01:56,431
Then you have reason to feel guilty too. Gosh, you...

38
00:01:56,531 --> 00:01:58,831
You bastard. What's that supposed to mean?

39
00:01:58,831 --> 00:02:00,361
Hey, hey, you...

40
00:02:00,361 --> 00:02:01,561
- Let go... - You bastard...

41
00:02:02,231 --> 00:02:03,771
- Father. - Dad.

42
00:02:04,931 --> 00:02:05,941
Darn it.

43
00:02:07,671 --> 00:02:08,671
Get out of the way.

44
00:02:09,971 --> 00:02:10,971
Darn it.

45
00:02:11,411 --> 00:02:14,041
What's wrong, Dad? What happened with President Ko?

46
00:02:15,911 --> 00:02:17,181
I'm sorry for startling you.

47
00:02:17,751 --> 00:02:19,021
I'm sorry to you too, Team Leader Ko.

48
00:02:20,021 --> 00:02:22,251
We're old classmates, and things just got heated.

49
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:24,351
We shouldn't be acting like this at the office.

50
00:02:25,321 --> 00:02:28,561
It's all right. By the way, is Chief Seo not here?

51
00:02:29,961 --> 00:02:31,361
Why are you looking for Chief Seo?

52
00:02:31,891 --> 00:02:34,931
General Director Ko just took an urgent call and left,

53
00:02:35,201 --> 00:02:38,001
and it sounded like something might have happened to Manager Seo.

54
00:02:40,501 --> 00:02:41,501
Actually,

55
00:02:42,941 --> 00:02:44,611
I heard Manager Seo had suddenly disappeared.

56
00:02:45,941 --> 00:02:48,641
- What? - What do you mean?

57
00:02:48,911 --> 00:02:50,481
Why would Manager Seo suddenly disappear?

58
00:02:53,251 --> 00:02:54,521
What's happening, Mother?

59
00:02:54,521 --> 00:02:55,691
Have you still not heard from Seung Ri?

60
00:02:55,791 --> 00:02:58,491
No. What should I do?

61
00:03:00,091 --> 00:03:01,791
I asked her to go to the hospital with me,

62
00:03:01,791 --> 00:03:04,091
but she said she'd go alone.

63
00:03:04,761 --> 00:03:06,501
I went grocery shopping to make some abalone porridge,

64
00:03:06,501 --> 00:03:07,631
and in that time...

65
00:03:07,961 --> 00:03:10,631
I've checked all the local hospitals and everywhere,

66
00:03:10,901 --> 00:03:12,341
but I couldn't find her.

67
00:03:13,171 --> 00:03:16,471
- Honey. - Honey, what are we going to do?

68
00:03:17,371 --> 00:03:18,571
Nothing bad has happened, right?

69
00:03:19,041 --> 00:03:21,441
Our Seung Ri will be all right, won't she? Right?

70
00:03:21,441 --> 00:03:23,311
Well, did she leave any kind of trace?

71
00:03:23,551 --> 00:03:26,381
Like a note or any sign of packing.

72
00:03:26,751 --> 00:03:27,821
A trace?

73
00:03:28,581 --> 00:03:29,851
There was nothing like that.

74
00:03:30,251 --> 00:03:33,091
- She tidied up her desk a bit... - Tidied her desk?

75
00:03:33,661 --> 00:03:34,761
What do you mean?

76
00:03:36,361 --> 00:03:38,861
I looked through it, thinking there might be a clue,

77
00:03:39,661 --> 00:03:41,561
but all the pictures of Gyeol were gone.

78
00:03:45,071 --> 00:03:47,901
Do you think she might have gone to see Gyeol?

79
00:03:48,001 --> 00:03:49,241
No, she didn't.

80
00:03:49,241 --> 00:03:51,641
Gyeol was with me at the office until just a little while ago.

81
00:03:53,711 --> 00:03:55,041
Please don't worry too much.

82
00:03:55,441 --> 00:03:58,881
You know how much Seung Ri has liked Gyeol all this time.

83
00:03:59,351 --> 00:04:02,181
She's probably trying to let go for good.

84
00:04:03,091 --> 00:04:04,351
I'll go out and look for her.

85
00:04:07,691 --> 00:04:10,431
You wait for Seung Ri at home. I'll go out.

86
00:04:10,691 --> 00:04:11,761
Where are you going?

87
00:04:11,831 --> 00:04:13,131
First, I'll go to the management office...

88
00:04:13,201 --> 00:04:14,801
and check the security footage from the garage.

89
00:04:15,161 --> 00:04:16,871
And I need to have the police run a search on her car.

90
00:04:19,541 --> 00:04:20,541
Seung Ri...

91
00:04:21,801 --> 00:04:23,511
Where on earth did you go?

92
00:04:30,981 --> 00:04:32,651
Tomorrow's finally the day.

93
00:04:33,051 --> 00:04:35,721
The day our joint webtoon, "The ER Witch," is released.

94
00:04:36,251 --> 00:04:39,691
Right. Good to know. Thanks.

95
00:04:40,961 --> 00:04:41,961
What was that?

96
00:04:42,361 --> 00:04:44,261
I mean, the first product of our collaboration...

97
00:04:44,261 --> 00:04:45,331
is launching tomorrow,

98
00:04:46,001 --> 00:04:47,301
and all you have to say is, "Good to know. Thanks."

99
00:04:48,261 --> 00:04:50,801
In case you'd forgotten,

100
00:04:50,931 --> 00:04:54,341
I'm saying thank you for telling me, as a humanitarian gesture.

101
00:04:54,401 --> 00:04:55,571
Unbelievable.

102
00:04:56,171 --> 00:05:00,181
Well, let me ask you something, just as a humanitarian gesture.

103
00:05:00,541 --> 00:05:01,781
About our bet on the view count.

104
00:05:02,281 --> 00:05:03,311
Why aren't you making a prediction?

105
00:05:03,381 --> 00:05:04,481
What's there to predict?

106
00:05:04,551 --> 00:05:06,281
We'll know when the results come out.

107
00:05:07,021 --> 00:05:09,951
Can't you at least make a humanitarian guess?

108
00:05:09,951 --> 00:05:10,951
Excuse me.

109
00:05:11,521 --> 00:05:14,261
I mean, you keep saying "humanitarian" over and over.

110
00:05:14,821 --> 00:05:16,061
Are you really going to keep this up?

111
00:05:16,061 --> 00:05:19,031
Why not? You, as a humanitarian gesture,

112
00:05:19,131 --> 00:05:21,161
went so far as to lie to my mother and say you liked me.

113
00:05:21,501 --> 00:05:23,571
So what? Am I not allowed to say it?

114
00:05:23,631 --> 00:05:25,841
A lie? When did I ever lie?

115
00:05:32,681 --> 00:05:33,681
Hi, Mom.

116
00:05:34,711 --> 00:05:36,751
Me? I haven't spoken to her today.

117
00:05:39,521 --> 00:05:42,081
What? Seo Seung Ri is missing?

118
00:05:44,351 --> 00:05:48,591
All right. I'm on my way. Darn it.

119
00:05:49,091 --> 00:05:51,061
What's wrong? What happened?

120
00:05:51,131 --> 00:05:53,701
Later. I'll explain later.

121
00:05:57,301 --> 00:05:59,801
Mom, is there a lot to do? Can I help?

122
00:06:00,071 --> 00:06:02,671
It's all right. I've already finished all the prep work,

123
00:06:02,911 --> 00:06:04,411
and I just need to marinate the meat.

124
00:06:04,471 --> 00:06:05,841
The rest can wait until tomorrow.

125
00:06:06,511 --> 00:06:08,341
It feels just like the day before a holiday.

126
00:06:08,341 --> 00:06:10,181
It's exciting. Don't you think so, Mom?

127
00:06:10,311 --> 00:06:11,381
I do too.

128
00:06:12,081 --> 00:06:15,821
I've gone my whole life without ever thinking I had parents,

129
00:06:16,221 --> 00:06:19,021
and now here I am, cooking because they're coming to visit.

130
00:06:19,861 --> 00:06:22,731
Mom, is there anything special you want to do with grandma?

131
00:06:23,291 --> 00:06:24,331
Something I want to do?

132
00:06:24,691 --> 00:06:26,561
After all the years you spent apart,

133
00:06:26,561 --> 00:06:28,161
there must be a lot you want to do together.

134
00:06:28,461 --> 00:06:29,471
Not really.

135
00:06:30,431 --> 00:06:32,001
Just being able to meet like this,

136
00:06:32,301 --> 00:06:36,771
share a nice meal, and talk is enough.

137
00:06:36,911 --> 00:06:38,941
Come on, don't say that. Think about it.

138
00:06:39,241 --> 00:06:41,811
Should I send you on a trip? Is there anywhere you want to go?

139
00:06:41,811 --> 00:06:43,151
A trip? Of course not.

140
00:06:44,551 --> 00:06:45,551
I just...

141
00:06:46,321 --> 00:06:48,521
I do want to sleep beside her for one night.

142
00:06:49,851 --> 00:06:51,851
When I was little and slept in my mother's arms,

143
00:06:52,251 --> 00:06:55,891
- her scent was so comforting. - What? Her scent?

144
00:06:56,361 --> 00:06:57,531
It's a real thing.

145
00:06:57,931 --> 00:07:00,231
A kind of fragrance that only a mother has.

146
00:07:01,531 --> 00:07:03,671
I really love my mom's scent too.

147
00:07:05,471 --> 00:07:08,341
I guess mothers have their own special scent.

148
00:07:08,901 --> 00:07:10,541
How could there be such a thing?

149
00:07:11,471 --> 00:07:13,741
It's probably just a good feeling because we were one body,

150
00:07:13,741 --> 00:07:15,681
connected by an umbilical cord.

151
00:07:17,681 --> 00:07:19,481
Is Dad asleep?

152
00:07:19,781 --> 00:07:22,251
I'm not sure. I think I saw him go out to the yard earlier.

153
00:07:22,381 --> 00:07:24,991
Why? Do you have something to say to him?

154
00:07:24,991 --> 00:07:26,091
No.

155
00:07:26,521 --> 00:07:28,891
Is something going on with Dad these days?

156
00:07:29,021 --> 00:07:30,091
What do you mean?

157
00:07:30,161 --> 00:07:33,461
It's just that he looks like he has something on his mind.

158
00:07:33,801 --> 00:07:35,901
What would he have to worry about?

159
00:07:38,331 --> 00:07:41,171
He does seem to be having trouble sleeping.

160
00:07:42,141 --> 00:07:45,881
But it's just his age. People sleep less as they get older.

161
00:07:56,751 --> 00:08:01,191
I guess you're starting to have some regrets too?

162
00:08:02,891 --> 00:08:04,791
You said it yourself back then.

163
00:08:04,791 --> 00:08:06,931
That you were the one who brought Gwon Sik to me.

164
00:08:07,631 --> 00:08:10,031
If so, it is only right that you feel some guilt.

165
00:08:16,441 --> 00:08:18,971
Father, are you still awake?

166
00:08:19,341 --> 00:08:21,741
Yes. I should be getting to bed.

167
00:08:21,741 --> 00:08:22,781
Father, wait.

168
00:08:23,881 --> 00:08:26,851
Did you and my father have some disagreement...

169
00:08:26,851 --> 00:08:28,981
regarding Eun Ae and me today?

170
00:08:29,291 --> 00:08:33,091
No, nothing like that. That is just how old classmates are.

171
00:08:33,491 --> 00:08:35,421
We may be old, but we are still childish...

172
00:08:35,491 --> 00:08:38,391
and pick fights like we are back in the old days.

173
00:08:39,031 --> 00:08:41,801
It has nothing to do with you two, so do not worry about it.

174
00:08:42,671 --> 00:08:43,671
Go on inside and get some sleep.

175
00:08:43,771 --> 00:08:46,501
- Yes, good night, Father. - Okay. You too.

176
00:08:51,341 --> 00:08:52,581
Eun Hyung, are you just getting in?

177
00:08:52,811 --> 00:08:55,081
Gyeol, why are you out here again?

178
00:08:55,981 --> 00:08:59,451
- Are you worried I can't sleep? - No, sir.

179
00:09:00,221 --> 00:09:02,791
I am sorry for constantly disturbing your sleep.

180
00:09:02,851 --> 00:09:04,491
It is not a disturbance.

181
00:09:05,151 --> 00:09:06,591
I am just very worried.

182
00:09:07,561 --> 00:09:10,361
Because it seems you have a dark tunnel inside of you...

183
00:09:10,361 --> 00:09:11,531
that you must escape.

184
00:09:12,931 --> 00:09:15,431
However, the fact that this painful memory...

185
00:09:15,501 --> 00:09:17,631
keeps haunting your dreams...

186
00:09:18,371 --> 00:09:21,601
might just be a sign that you are now able to overcome it.

187
00:09:22,141 --> 00:09:23,141
You really think so?

188
00:09:23,671 --> 00:09:27,741
As always, you give a clear answer to my troubled mind.

189
00:09:28,441 --> 00:09:29,681
Was I that clear?

190
00:09:30,411 --> 00:09:31,411
Well, I am relieved.

191
00:09:41,561 --> 00:09:42,861
Seung Ri...

192
00:09:43,561 --> 00:09:45,861
found out about her father's past.

193
00:09:46,731 --> 00:09:47,761
Seung Ri did.

194
00:09:48,961 --> 00:09:51,531
I have a really bad feeling about this. Seriously.

195
00:09:54,201 --> 00:09:55,201
Oh my gosh.

196
00:09:55,911 --> 00:09:57,811
You scared me.

197
00:09:58,211 --> 00:10:01,611
Give me a break. I was the one who was more scared.

198
00:10:01,981 --> 00:10:04,481
But what are you doing in here with the lights off?

199
00:10:05,251 --> 00:10:07,981
Your husband was just trying to do some thinking.

200
00:10:08,351 --> 00:10:10,551
I mean, your husband is trying to be lost in thought,

201
00:10:10,621 --> 00:10:12,691
and you couldn't even wait a moment before running in here.

202
00:10:12,991 --> 00:10:15,061
Lost in thought? Let me see your face, dear.

203
00:10:17,361 --> 00:10:21,531
My, my. You look like you have seen a ghost, dear.

204
00:10:21,601 --> 00:10:23,331
But really, what is wrong?

205
00:10:23,601 --> 00:10:24,601
What is going on?

206
00:10:24,671 --> 00:10:27,601
Why do you have such a long face all the time lately?

207
00:10:27,871 --> 00:10:29,071
Look, Eun Su Jung...

208
00:10:29,511 --> 00:10:31,511
I know he is still alive,

209
00:10:31,841 --> 00:10:34,011
but we held a live funeral for my father.

210
00:10:34,411 --> 00:10:36,751
Didn't you ever think about how much pain his only son must be in?

211
00:10:36,851 --> 00:10:38,951
Did that thought never even cross your mind?

212
00:10:39,011 --> 00:10:41,581
My goodness. Is that why you have been so worried about Father,

213
00:10:41,651 --> 00:10:43,491
looking like you are on death's door every day?

214
00:10:44,051 --> 00:10:46,121
My goodness. To think Father does not recognise...

215
00:10:46,121 --> 00:10:47,491
what a devoted son you are.

216
00:10:47,961 --> 00:10:51,691
Yes, I am suffering. Now that you know, just go to bed.

217
00:10:51,891 --> 00:10:53,531
I am just going to think for a little while longer...

218
00:10:53,601 --> 00:10:54,961
Why do you keep forgetting, honey?

219
00:10:55,231 --> 00:10:57,571
Do you not know I can't sleep without your arm around me?

220
00:10:57,671 --> 00:10:58,971
Hurry up and come.

221
00:11:00,241 --> 00:11:01,841
All right, I will be right there.

222
00:11:02,841 --> 00:11:04,871
Can a man not even think by himself for a minute?

223
00:11:04,941 --> 00:11:06,241
I really have a lot on my mind.

224
00:11:06,911 --> 00:11:08,541
My arm falls asleep so easily these days.

225
00:11:10,611 --> 00:11:13,821
Oh, by the way, has Min Ho come home yet?

226
00:11:14,081 --> 00:11:15,881
I do not think so. It looks like he is not back yet.

227
00:11:16,921 --> 00:11:17,921
That boy.

228
00:11:17,991 --> 00:11:20,161
He is probably out wandering around looking for Seung Ri again.

229
00:11:20,461 --> 00:11:23,091
Looking for Seung Ri? Where did Seung Ri go?

230
00:11:23,761 --> 00:11:27,101
Seung Ri? Oh, she probably went home.

231
00:11:27,161 --> 00:11:28,501
And he is probably following her around again,

232
00:11:28,501 --> 00:11:29,701
trying to walk her home.

233
00:11:30,471 --> 00:11:34,601
Honey, lately, I keep getting a bad feeling.

234
00:11:35,101 --> 00:11:37,541
They say no parent can win against their own child.

235
00:11:38,141 --> 00:11:39,341
At this rate, eventually,

236
00:11:39,781 --> 00:11:42,311
I feel like Seung Ri is going to become our daughter-in-law.

237
00:11:42,781 --> 00:11:44,551
It is like father, like son.

238
00:11:44,551 --> 00:11:46,951
Father was devoted to Mother, and you are devoted to me,

239
00:11:47,021 --> 00:11:48,251
and Min Ho is completely devoted to Seung Ri.

240
00:11:48,251 --> 00:11:50,351
It's just devotion to one person.

241
00:11:50,821 --> 00:11:53,161
It is in his blood. How can he fight it?

242
00:11:53,221 --> 00:11:55,691
Seriously, please stop saying such ridiculous things.

243
00:11:56,231 --> 00:11:59,261
I'd rather have Min Ho live and die a bachelor...

244
00:11:59,761 --> 00:12:02,201
than become in-laws with Seo Gwon Sik.

245
00:12:02,201 --> 00:12:03,701
Over my dead body.

246
00:12:04,031 --> 00:12:06,041
Don't you think you're being too harsh?

247
00:12:06,671 --> 00:12:10,471
What if our one and only precious son, Min Ho,

248
00:12:10,611 --> 00:12:12,111
turns his back on us for the rest of his life?

249
00:12:13,041 --> 00:12:14,281
Oh, honestly.

250
00:12:14,881 --> 00:12:17,611
Here, take my arm. Come on, let's get some sleep.

251
00:12:20,121 --> 00:12:22,481
By the way, Father and Mother were invited...

252
00:12:22,551 --> 00:12:24,621
to their daughter's house tomorrow.

253
00:12:25,191 --> 00:12:26,221
Their "daughter's" house?

254
00:12:27,321 --> 00:12:28,861
You mean Secretary Jo's house?

255
00:12:28,921 --> 00:12:32,091
Yes. I mean, I can understand Mother going,

256
00:12:32,231 --> 00:12:35,331
but why does Father like that family so much too?

257
00:12:35,761 --> 00:12:37,701
What if Father ends up giving his remaining 20 percent shares,

258
00:12:38,131 --> 00:12:40,241
all to that family?

259
00:12:40,501 --> 00:12:41,841
Oh, that's ridiculous.

260
00:12:42,271 --> 00:12:45,171
They aren't even legally entitled to an inheritance.

261
00:12:45,241 --> 00:12:46,811
You think the law is everything?

262
00:12:46,941 --> 00:12:48,381
If Father states in his will...

263
00:12:48,441 --> 00:12:50,911
that he's giving his remaining shares to Kang Yeon Ja,

264
00:12:50,981 --> 00:12:52,751
it'll be over. It only takes that one sentence.

265
00:12:53,851 --> 00:12:55,721
No, I can't let this happen.

266
00:12:55,921 --> 00:12:58,251
I have to follow them to that house tomorrow.

267
00:12:58,521 --> 00:13:02,261
- What are you going to do there? - What do you mean, what will I do?

268
00:13:02,621 --> 00:13:04,531
I'm going to stand guard...

269
00:13:04,591 --> 00:13:07,601
and make sure they can't even mention shares or inheritance.

270
00:13:08,561 --> 00:13:10,471
Crystal, you're really...

271
00:13:11,001 --> 00:13:14,641
I'm Nongae. No matter what it takes,

272
00:13:14,901 --> 00:13:16,971
I will protect the kingdom of Ko Dae Chi. Just you watch.

273
00:13:17,811 --> 00:13:21,841
Eun Su Jung, I love you so much. Let's protect it together.

274
00:13:22,511 --> 00:13:25,951
- The Ko Dae Chi Kingdom. - The Ko Dae Chi Kingdom.

275
00:14:37,291 --> 00:14:39,451
(You've worked so hard, Seung Ri. Good luck on your CSAT! Gyeol.)

276
00:15:20,701 --> 00:15:21,701
I'm sorry.

277
00:15:25,871 --> 00:15:26,901
Gyeol.

278
00:15:30,011 --> 00:15:31,241
I'm so sorry.

279
00:15:32,611 --> 00:15:33,611
I'm sorry.

280
00:15:48,661 --> 00:15:50,891
(Gangsu Construction)

281
00:15:52,161 --> 00:15:54,001
Where in the world are you, Seo Seung Ri?

282
00:15:54,361 --> 00:15:55,861
I've checked everywhere you might be.

283
00:15:56,971 --> 00:15:59,771
Please be okay. Please.

284
00:16:01,471 --> 00:16:03,171
(Seung Ri)

285
00:16:04,571 --> 00:16:07,311
Seo Seung Ri. Where are you right now?

286
00:16:09,481 --> 00:16:11,981
What? Where is that?

287
00:16:12,981 --> 00:16:15,721
Okay. I'll head over right now.

288
00:16:16,251 --> 00:16:18,091
Yes, thank you. Thank you so much.

289
00:16:22,191 --> 00:16:23,331
Is that really true?

290
00:16:24,561 --> 00:16:29,261
Okay, I understand. What about Seung Ri? Is she okay?

291
00:16:31,471 --> 00:16:34,201
Thank you, Son-in-law Ko. Thank you so much.

292
00:16:35,441 --> 00:16:37,371
Honey, they found her.

293
00:16:37,911 --> 00:16:40,081
Son-in-law Ko found our Seung Ri.

294
00:16:40,511 --> 00:16:43,711
- That's a relief. - Where? Where did they find her?

295
00:16:44,051 --> 00:16:45,351
I don't know the details.

296
00:16:45,411 --> 00:16:47,951
He called while he was driving to meet Seung Ri.

297
00:16:48,381 --> 00:16:50,321
Is she hurt? Is she okay?

298
00:16:50,791 --> 00:16:53,691
He didn't say otherwise, so I assume she's fine.

299
00:16:54,161 --> 00:16:56,161
He said he'll call as soon as he sees Seung Ri.

300
00:16:56,491 --> 00:16:59,191
What a relief. I'm so relieved.

301
00:17:00,061 --> 00:17:02,301
Still, what's going on with Seo Seung Ri?

302
00:17:02,731 --> 00:17:04,101
What could have possibly happened...

303
00:17:04,101 --> 00:17:05,631
to make the world's most perfect student...

304
00:17:05,701 --> 00:17:06,701
suddenly run away from home?

305
00:17:07,241 --> 00:17:08,241
Honey,

306
00:17:08,901 --> 00:17:10,511
we should go too.

307
00:17:10,811 --> 00:17:13,811
I'll call Son-in-law Ko back and ask for the address.

308
00:17:14,141 --> 00:17:15,811
Instead of just waiting at home,

309
00:17:16,141 --> 00:17:18,151
I think it would be better for us to go get her ourselves.

310
00:17:18,451 --> 00:17:19,821
General Director Ko said he'd bring her.

311
00:17:20,221 --> 00:17:21,251
Just wait.

312
00:17:22,421 --> 00:17:23,751
Honestly, that man.

313
00:17:24,021 --> 00:17:25,721
I mean, any other time,

314
00:17:25,791 --> 00:17:27,721
he'd be the first one to rush out the door.

315
00:17:28,761 --> 00:17:29,831
I know, right?

316
00:17:30,261 --> 00:17:33,061
Why is Dad acting like this about Seung Ri? Seriously.

317
00:17:59,451 --> 00:18:01,121
You're the one who called this morning, right?

318
00:18:01,361 --> 00:18:02,521
Where is she now?

319
00:18:02,761 --> 00:18:05,091
She's inside. She's asleep right now.

320
00:18:05,391 --> 00:18:08,461
- How is she? Is she okay? - Yes, I think so.

321
00:18:09,001 --> 00:18:10,001
That's a relief.

322
00:18:10,001 --> 00:18:12,601
Could you tell me where and how you found her?

323
00:18:12,701 --> 00:18:15,101
Last night, she showed up looking like...

324
00:18:15,171 --> 00:18:16,741
she was about to collapse...

325
00:18:16,971 --> 00:18:18,811
and asked if she could stay for the night,

326
00:18:19,271 --> 00:18:20,911
so I gave her a room.

327
00:18:21,441 --> 00:18:23,011
But this morning, she was nowhere to be seen.

328
00:18:23,011 --> 00:18:25,751
I thought it was odd, so I looked around.

329
00:18:26,011 --> 00:18:28,081
I found her collapsed from exhaustion.

330
00:18:28,481 --> 00:18:31,451
I saw your number on her phone, so I called you.

331
00:18:32,051 --> 00:18:34,421
Thank you. Thank you so much.

332
00:18:35,461 --> 00:18:36,531
Yes.

333
00:18:59,451 --> 00:19:01,851
Why are you here all alone like this?

334
00:19:02,481 --> 00:19:04,291
I was so worried about you.

335
00:19:08,861 --> 00:19:09,861
Seung Ri.

336
00:19:10,591 --> 00:19:13,231
Thank you for being safe.

337
00:19:13,661 --> 00:19:15,301
I'm so thankful you're here.

338
00:19:16,871 --> 00:19:17,971
Thank you, Seung Ri.

339
00:19:22,071 --> 00:19:23,241
Min Ho?

340
00:19:24,271 --> 00:19:25,441
Seung Ri.

341
00:19:26,071 --> 00:19:27,141
Do you recognise me?

342
00:19:31,051 --> 00:19:34,381
I'm here now, so don't worry about anything, okay?

343
00:19:34,981 --> 00:19:38,291
From now on, I'll never leave you alone. Never.

344
00:19:40,591 --> 00:19:41,621
But now,

345
00:19:42,991 --> 00:19:45,131
I have nowhere left to go.

346
00:19:47,801 --> 00:19:49,901
My whole world has fallen apart.

347
00:19:53,571 --> 00:19:54,671
Only you, Min Ho...

348
00:19:57,711 --> 00:19:59,311
Only you are still the same.

349
00:20:00,811 --> 00:20:02,011
What are you talking about?

350
00:20:02,781 --> 00:20:04,381
Why would you say your world has fallen apart?

351
00:20:05,651 --> 00:20:06,681
Min Ho.

352
00:20:07,581 --> 00:20:08,951
Please take me with you.

353
00:20:10,451 --> 00:20:12,221
I don't care where.

354
00:20:13,221 --> 00:20:15,761
Somewhere far, far away.

355
00:20:17,961 --> 00:20:19,631
Please just take me with you.

356
00:20:21,661 --> 00:20:22,801
Okay, Seung Ri.

357
00:20:23,331 --> 00:20:25,131
I'll take you wherever you want to go,

358
00:20:25,401 --> 00:20:27,141
so don't you worry, okay?

359
00:20:39,351 --> 00:20:41,181
How is she?

360
00:20:41,821 --> 00:20:43,121
Is there anything else wrong?

361
00:20:44,051 --> 00:20:45,591
Okay.

362
00:20:45,891 --> 00:20:50,231
I've just packed a small bag. I'll head straight to the hospital.

363
00:20:50,591 --> 00:20:51,791
Okay. I'm hanging up.

364
00:20:52,361 --> 00:20:54,231
What happened? Is she okay?

365
00:20:54,601 --> 00:20:57,201
Yes, but she's been admitted to the hospital.

366
00:20:57,401 --> 00:20:59,231
She's on an IV for exhaustion.

367
00:20:59,971 --> 00:21:01,901
What is going on? Honestly, Seung Ri.

368
00:21:02,641 --> 00:21:05,911
Mom, wait. Let me go with you. I'll just go change.

369
00:21:05,971 --> 00:21:09,011
They said nothing else is wrong. You should get some sleep.

370
00:21:09,281 --> 00:21:11,951
You were up all night looking for your sister.

371
00:21:12,011 --> 00:21:14,351
Did anyone in this family get any sleep last night?

372
00:21:14,351 --> 00:21:16,521
- I'm going with you. - If you have that much energy,

373
00:21:16,591 --> 00:21:18,221
go to your studio and get some work done.

374
00:21:18,691 --> 00:21:20,691
Isn't your webtoon launching?

375
00:21:20,691 --> 00:21:22,421
That's beside the point.

376
00:21:22,491 --> 00:21:25,761
She needs to rest quietly. Just listen to me.

377
00:21:29,901 --> 00:21:30,901
Honey.

378
00:21:31,471 --> 00:21:32,571
Right, I understand.

379
00:21:33,401 --> 00:21:34,601
I'll head over there now...

380
00:21:35,971 --> 00:21:38,741
Actually, no. I'll just stay here and work.

381
00:21:39,571 --> 00:21:41,881
Go check on her and call me back.

382
00:21:42,811 --> 00:21:43,811
Okay.

383
00:21:52,151 --> 00:21:53,391
I'm sorry, Seung Ri.

384
00:21:55,561 --> 00:21:56,931
It's all because of your pathetic father.

385
00:22:01,561 --> 00:22:02,561
Gwon Sik.

386
00:22:03,201 --> 00:22:04,301
How is Manager Seo?

387
00:22:05,431 --> 00:22:07,971
She's at the hospital recovering.

388
00:22:09,271 --> 00:22:11,311
Oh, that's a relief.

389
00:22:11,911 --> 00:22:13,511
Thank goodness it wasn't worse.

390
00:22:15,041 --> 00:22:18,181
My daughter collapsed because of me and is lying in a hospital bed,

391
00:22:19,411 --> 00:22:20,651
and I can't even go see her.

392
00:22:32,061 --> 00:22:33,191
After all this,

393
00:22:34,431 --> 00:22:35,601
can I even call myself a father?

394
00:22:39,201 --> 00:22:40,671
Am I even human?

395
00:22:48,641 --> 00:22:49,681
She's okay?

396
00:22:50,311 --> 00:22:53,111
That's a relief. Is she hurt anywhere else?

397
00:22:54,051 --> 00:22:55,781
Okay, alright.

398
00:22:57,651 --> 00:22:58,891
Was that General Director Ko?

399
00:22:58,891 --> 00:23:00,921
Did Manager Seo make it home safely?

400
00:23:01,461 --> 00:23:02,621
She's at the hospital.

401
00:23:02,891 --> 00:23:04,791
She collapsed from exhaustion and is on an IV.

402
00:23:04,791 --> 00:23:06,061
It seems she's fine otherwise.

403
00:23:06,861 --> 00:23:07,961
That's such a relief.

404
00:23:08,961 --> 00:23:12,301
But what do you think is really going on with Manager Seo?

405
00:23:12,871 --> 00:23:17,241
At Grandfather's living funeral, and the day we had drinks together,

406
00:23:17,371 --> 00:23:18,871
she seemed perfectly fine.

407
00:23:19,371 --> 00:23:22,381
I know. But at least Min Ho is with Seung Ri,

408
00:23:22,441 --> 00:23:25,081
- so it's a huge relief. - It is.

409
00:23:25,351 --> 00:23:27,681
General Director Ko is really amazing.

410
00:23:28,021 --> 00:23:30,291
I don't know how he can be so steadfast.

411
00:23:30,791 --> 00:23:32,321
He's been like that since we were little.

412
00:23:32,321 --> 00:23:34,191
Though he expressed it differently.

413
00:23:34,961 --> 00:23:35,961
How so?

414
00:23:36,691 --> 00:23:38,731
You know, like picking on someone for no reason.

415
00:23:38,891 --> 00:23:41,201
If Seung Ri and I were studying in the garden,

416
00:23:41,201 --> 00:23:44,671
he'd throw a basketball on the table or spill juice on purpose.

417
00:23:45,101 --> 00:23:47,041
- What? Really? - Yes.

418
00:23:47,801 --> 00:23:50,441
But should we really be waiting here like this?

419
00:23:51,141 --> 00:23:53,741
I know she wouldn't want us to see her while she's sick, but...

420
00:23:53,811 --> 00:23:56,011
He said he'll watch her and contact us,

421
00:23:56,081 --> 00:23:57,881
- so let's just wait. - Okay.

422
00:24:01,021 --> 00:24:02,251
It's the family group chat.

423
00:24:03,151 --> 00:24:04,551
Your mom says...

424
00:24:04,551 --> 00:24:06,551
dinner with Grandfather and Grandmother is at 7pm...

425
00:24:06,621 --> 00:24:07,621
and not to be late.

426
00:24:07,961 --> 00:24:09,521
I got the message too.

427
00:24:10,491 --> 00:24:13,601
Yes, Mother. I'll leave work on the dot and come help.

428
00:24:14,261 --> 00:24:15,561
How can you be so happy about it?

429
00:24:16,501 --> 00:24:19,171
Of course. After my father passed away,

430
00:24:19,631 --> 00:24:21,871
I've never really felt like I belonged anywhere.

431
00:24:22,901 --> 00:24:26,211
Well, from now on, you'll feel it until you're sick of it.

432
00:24:26,811 --> 00:24:30,011
You'll learn that sense of belonging isn't always a good thing.

433
00:24:32,281 --> 00:24:34,481
Grandma, I'm home from preschool.

434
00:24:34,481 --> 00:24:36,451
Welcome back. Did you have a good day?

435
00:24:36,721 --> 00:24:38,651
Are we having another party...

436
00:24:38,651 --> 00:24:40,221
because Great-Grandma and Great-Grandpa are coming over?

437
00:24:40,821 --> 00:24:43,561
A party? Yes, that's right. It's a party.

438
00:24:43,661 --> 00:24:46,091
I love having parties all the time, Grandma.

439
00:24:46,291 --> 00:24:47,801
I'm going to wash my hands.

440
00:24:49,861 --> 00:24:51,701
You can't join us for dinner tonight, right?

441
00:24:52,031 --> 00:24:54,341
I probably won't be back until late tonight.

442
00:24:54,701 --> 00:24:55,801
Maybe next time.

443
00:24:57,141 --> 00:25:00,241
Grandma, Dad, I'm going to go play at Aunt Cho Rong's.

444
00:25:00,381 --> 00:25:02,241
You should have a snack before you go.

445
00:25:02,311 --> 00:25:04,551
Auntie said she'd make me cheese Mung Bean Pancakes.

446
00:25:05,281 --> 00:25:09,251
- But Dad, what's that? - This? You'll find out soon.

447
00:25:10,291 --> 00:25:11,951
- I'm going now. - Okay.

448
00:25:12,021 --> 00:25:13,021
I'm heading out.

449
00:25:15,391 --> 00:25:17,731
Bit Na is getting too attached to Cho Rong.

450
00:25:20,231 --> 00:25:23,401
- Hi, Auntie. - Welcome, Bit Na.

451
00:25:25,671 --> 00:25:26,701
Hey, watch out.

452
00:25:33,471 --> 00:25:35,781
Hey, are you okay?

453
00:25:36,281 --> 00:25:37,381
Yes.

454
00:25:38,111 --> 00:25:41,551
You have to be careful. That was a close call.

455
00:25:42,921 --> 00:25:44,521
Auntie, are you hurt?

456
00:25:45,021 --> 00:25:47,321
I'm not hurt. I'm perfectly fine.

457
00:25:47,361 --> 00:25:51,561
That's a relief. Oh, here.

458
00:25:52,331 --> 00:25:53,461
What's this?

459
00:25:53,861 --> 00:25:54,861
A scarf.

460
00:25:55,161 --> 00:25:57,801
You lent me your scarf the other day when I had a nosebleed.

461
00:25:58,471 --> 00:25:59,831
I was going to wash it and give it back,

462
00:25:59,901 --> 00:26:02,401
but I bought you a new one. I really appreciated it back then.

463
00:26:03,501 --> 00:26:07,011
- Aren't you going to take it? - Oh, thank you.

464
00:26:08,011 --> 00:26:10,611
Bit Na, play for a little bit and then head straight home, okay?

465
00:26:10,681 --> 00:26:11,681
I'm off to teach class.

466
00:26:11,811 --> 00:26:14,781
- Bye-bye, Daddy. - I'm off, Cho Rong.

467
00:26:16,281 --> 00:26:17,551
- Oh, dear. - Hello, ma'am.

468
00:26:17,621 --> 00:26:20,021
- Oh, heading to work? - Yes. See you later.

469
00:26:20,221 --> 00:26:21,721
Hello, Grandma.

470
00:26:21,791 --> 00:26:24,931
Oh, Bit Na, you're here. Gosh, it's so hot.

471
00:26:24,991 --> 00:26:27,931
Cho Rong, bring me a glass of cold water.

472
00:26:28,361 --> 00:26:29,631
Gosh, I'm boiling.

473
00:26:32,531 --> 00:26:35,101
I asked you to bring me a glass of cold water.

474
00:26:35,101 --> 00:26:36,641
Didn't you hear me?

475
00:26:37,511 --> 00:26:42,011
Goodness. She's completely spaced out.

476
00:26:42,711 --> 00:26:45,551
Bit Na, what's wrong with your Auntie Cho Rong?

477
00:26:46,181 --> 00:26:47,321
I don't know.

478
00:26:47,321 --> 00:26:51,021
My dad saved her, so she didn't get hit by the pot.

479
00:26:51,351 --> 00:26:52,591
Your dad saved her?

480
00:26:52,851 --> 00:26:54,021
What do you mean by that?

481
00:26:55,291 --> 00:26:56,721
Thank you so much, General Director Ko.

482
00:26:57,331 --> 00:26:59,231
I don't know what I would've done without you.

483
00:27:00,701 --> 00:27:01,701
Not at all.

484
00:27:03,031 --> 00:27:04,831
Chief Seo...

485
00:27:05,931 --> 00:27:08,371
I think something happened to Seung Ri.

486
00:27:09,801 --> 00:27:11,311
If you know anything about it,

487
00:27:11,911 --> 00:27:13,611
would you please tell me?

488
00:27:14,741 --> 00:27:15,981
I can't stand to see Seung Ri struggling...

489
00:27:16,041 --> 00:27:17,051
like this anymore.

490
00:27:18,411 --> 00:27:23,021
I'll take care of everything, so please tell me. I'm begging you.

491
00:27:25,291 --> 00:27:26,291
Hey, Ko Min Ho.

492
00:27:27,121 --> 00:27:28,121
What are you talking about?

493
00:27:28,191 --> 00:27:29,891
What do you mean you'll take care of everything?

494
00:27:30,261 --> 00:27:32,461
- Father. - Get out. Get out. Now.

495
00:27:34,201 --> 00:27:36,001
General Director Ko, please leave.

496
00:27:37,531 --> 00:27:39,701
I need to speak with your father.

497
00:27:50,781 --> 00:27:51,781
Ko Dae Chi.

498
00:27:52,911 --> 00:27:53,921
Ko Dae Chi?

499
00:27:54,621 --> 00:27:56,651
So I guess everyone and their mother thinks...

500
00:27:56,651 --> 00:27:58,651
they can disrespect me now.

501
00:27:59,451 --> 00:28:00,921
I'm going to turn myself in.

502
00:28:02,391 --> 00:28:04,331
What? What did you just say?

503
00:28:05,591 --> 00:28:06,591
Turn yourself in?

504
00:28:29,181 --> 00:28:32,121
(Our Happy Days)
